Original commit body from a5557d6be856bb46a0c799cb7f93d06769c3d05f:

The Woodpecker full-suite and nightly pipelines run pytest
packages/*/tests/ but never installed hypergumbo-lang-scip-python or
measured its coverage. Its tests passed there by accident:
test_adjudication_packet.py loads scripts/measure-taint-precision.py at
collection time, and that script puts every packages/*/src on sys.path.
Reproduced in a clean env without the package: collecting its tests
alone gives 5 ImportErrors; collecting core's tests first makes them
import, and bisection over core's test files isolates that one file.
So the package ran uninstalled (no entry point), unmeasured, and one
unrelated edit away from collection errors. Both steps now install it
and add its --cov path; check-package-coverage scip-python is 100%.

Lint scanners, measured rather than assumed:
- check-docstring-drift DID skip scip-python (hand-kept DEFAULT_SCOPE);
  it now globs packages/*/src: default co-change scan 352 -> 359 files.
- check-id-construction, check-pass-id-agreement,
  check-multi-value-field-axis-declaration, check-recorded-producer-input
  kept the same list only as a sys.path import fallback; they scan by
  glob or discover analyzers via entry points, so they missed nothing.
  They glob now too, so there is no list to forget. All four exit 0.

tests/test_ci_package_lists.py derives the package set from the tree
and pins: every Woodpecker step whose pytest runs packages/*/tests/
installs every package and measures exactly cov-paths.sh's sources, and
each linter (run in a subprocess, so its sys.path edits cannot leak)
puts every packages/*/src on its path. Mutation-checked: the old
full-suite.yml fails 2, the old check-pass-id-agreement fails 1.

Not changed: .github/workflows copies (GitHub Actions is disabled under
Woodpecker CI per scripts/ci-debug); the self-tree-validation,
self-claims-gate and integration steps, which run no package tests.

Addresses WI-bavak.

